=== CORE ===

This is the Core directory. No external dependencies should be introduced here.
Core <-- Interpreter <-- Scripts where 'a <-- b' means 'b depends (or can depend) upon a.'

The Core directory abides by the following rules without exception:

I: Any approved external dependencies must be able to be compiled into a single static riscv32 lib

II: Any code must be fully portable between riscv32 & the supported unix-based platforms

III: All bindings (E.g. wrappers exposing libs to python via ctypes/cffi) must live here

IV: The rules for introducing bindings are as follows:

    - If the python binding is purely exposing functions to be used in the interpreter (I.e. for speed / memory savings) place it under ```python```.

    - Otherwise, if the binding is targeting a native implementation (I.e. can be expected to run on the softcore) introduce it under the respective subdirectory (E.g. ```libs```)

You will need to have the risc-v-gnu-toolchain installed in order to compile for the softcore target (E.g. 32-bit based RISCV NERV processor) which you build with ```make riscv```.

By default ```make``` will only target supported unix-based systems.
